# r1113 P11 regression, world pwgperf: the Power Grid performance rows SQ-PWG-01 to -05, -07 and -08 (queue section
# "SQ-PWG Power Grid performance measuring"; D14 and H7 inputs, energy_advanced.md "P11 evaluation"). Target jar
# jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar (sha1 cbc2ddee37ca; a later fix build replaces it).
# PERF SESSION REQUIRED: open one (tools/perf/session/perf_session.sh) with JFR on before the boot; qrun marks each row
# id in it, so the mean / p99 tick per row comes from the session report (no pass line reads JFR in-batch).
# Fresh group A superflat, level pwgperf, spawn-animals=false. Nothing else runs on this server during the batch.
# Areas (each row forceloads its own and removes the previous one, so earlier grids PAUSE and do not add to the next
# row's cost; queue rows used one origin for all ladders, moved here so no grid is built over another):
#   -02 ladder 25 at 1000 -60 1000 (X 1000-1040, Z 1000-1005) | -03 ladder 100 at 1000 -60 1100 (Z 1100-1115)
#   -04 ladder 500 at 1000 -60 1200 (Z 1200-1275) | -05 20 grids of 25 at 1000 -60 1400 (X 1000-1990, Z 1400-1405)
#   -07 generator and motor (SQ-PWG-38 A and B, P4 coordinates X 1090-1140, Z 1140-1260)
# Prep: COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-17.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwgperf A
#   for p in pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe; do cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/$p.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$p.js; done
#   Default powergrid configs. perfBot jar present in OUT/srv/mods (SQ-PWG-08).
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113pwg/pwgperf.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwgperf
# SQ-PWG-08 caveat: perfBot bots have no client, so they never send NegotiateSyncC2SPacket / EndpointTrackingC2SPacket;
# the row gives the server tick with 40 players near the grid, not per-bot network use. Network numbers and the
# syncWithDoubles / clientMirror comparison come from the owner rows CQ-PWG-01 to -04. If `pbot` exposes sent bytes,
# record them; the two config reruns of the queue text are left out (they need real clients to mean anything).
pace 2

## SQ-PWG-01 | baseline: no grid, 5 min idle (perf segment)
> forceload add 992 992 1100 1100
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> weather clear
sleep 30
> forge tps
sleep 300
> forge tps
> powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld
sleep 3
reject An unexpected error occurred
look record mean / p99 tick of this segment from the perf session (baseline for -02 to -07); counter near 0 us or "no measurement"

## SQ-PWG-02 | ladder 25 (about 50 nodes), 5 min
> zpwgg ladder 1000 -60 1000 25
waitlog \[zpwgg\] ladder built n=25 30
sleep 10
> zpwgg net 1002 -60 1000
sleep 300
> powergrid performance get NetSolve
> powergrid performance get JavaMNA
> powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld
> forge tps
sleep 3
expect \[zpwgg\] net paused=false
reject An unexpected error occurred
reject Converged after
look mean tick delta against SQ-PWG-01 under 0.1 ms; networkNodes about 50; record the three counters (min / max / avg us)

## SQ-PWG-03 | ladder 100 (about 200 nodes), 5 min; -02's area unloaded first
> forceload remove 992 992 1100 1100
> forceload add 992 1095 1050 1120
sleep 5
> zpwgg ladder 1000 -60 1100 100
waitlog \[zpwgg\] ladder built n=100 30
sleep 10
> zpwgg net 1002 -60 1100
sleep 300
> powergrid performance get NetSolve
> powergrid performance get JavaMNA
> powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld
> forge tps
sleep 3
expect \[zpwgg\] net paused=false
reject An unexpected error occurred
look mean tick delta under 1 ms; about 200 nodes; record the counters

## SQ-PWG-04 | ladder 500 (about 1000 nodes), 5 min
> forceload remove 992 1095 1050 1120
> forceload add 992 1195 1050 1280
sleep 5
> zpwgg ladder 1000 -60 1200 500
waitlog \[zpwgg\] ladder built n=500 60
sleep 10
> zpwgg net 1002 -60 1200
sleep 300
> powergrid performance get NetSolve
> powergrid performance get JavaMNA
> powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld
> forge tps
sleep 3
expect \[zpwgg\] net paused=false
reject An unexpected error occurred
look recorded (scaling curve, no pass line); compare with the offline harness (0.11 ms per changed solve, 9 ms first solve, 1000-node ladder)

## SQ-PWG-05 | 20 separate 50-node grids, 5 min
> forceload remove 992 1195 1050 1280
> forceload add 992 1395 2000 1410
sleep 10
> zpwgg grids 1000 -60 1400 20 25
waitlog \[zpwgg\] grids built count=20 60
sleep 10
> zpwgg net 1002 -60 1400
sleep 300
> powergrid performance get NetSolve
> powergrid performance get minecraft:overworld
> forge tps
sleep 3
reject An unexpected error occurred
look total delta recorded; about 20 x SQ-PWG-02's delta (linear in grid count)

## SQ-PWG-07pre | forceload P4 area; unload -05; build SQ-PWG-38 A (motor, 4 presses) (setup, from r1113/pwg5.qb SQ-PWG-38)
> forceload remove 992 1395 2000 1410
> forceload add 1090 1140 1140 1260
sleep 10
> zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1160 258
waitlog \[zpwg3\] done 20
> zpwg3 place 1103 -60 1160 powergrid:current_gauge
> zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1160 powergrid:electric_motor facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1106 -60 1162 powergrid:voltage_gauge
> zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1160 0 1103 -60 1160 0
> zpwg3 w 1103 -60 1160 1 1106 -60 1160 0
> zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1160 1 1100 -60 1160 1
> zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1160 0 1106 -60 1162 0
> zpwg3 w 1106 -60 1160 1 1106 -60 1162 1
sleep 2
> zpwg4 kin 1106 -60 1160
> zpwg3 be 1103 -60 1160
> zpwg3 be 1106 -60 1162
> zpwg3 place 1107 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1108 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1109 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1110 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
sleep 2
> zpwg4 kin 1107 -60 1160
> zpwg4 kin 1106 -60 1160
> zpwg3 be 1103 -60 1160
> zpwg3 be 1106 -60 1162
> zpwg3 place 1111 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1112 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1113 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1114 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1115 -60 1160 create:mechanical_press facing=east
sleep 2
> zpwg4 kin 1107 -60 1160
> zpwg4 kin 1106 -60 1160
> zpwg3 be 1103 -60 1160
> zpwg3 be 1106 -60 1162
expect \[zpwg4\] speed=255 .*generated=255 overstressed
expect \[zpwg4\] network capacitySU=16320 stressSU=0 members
expect \[zpwg4\] .*overstressed=true
reject \[zpwg\w*\] error
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look record RPM, SU, V, A per step: 0 presses about 0.50 A at 258 V; 4 presses stressSU = 4 x k x 255 (8160 at k = 8), current = Vm / (25.6 / (4k / 64)) (about 5.0 A, 10 %); 9 presses overstressed, current about Vm / 25.6 (about 10 A)

## SQ-PWG-SETUP12P4 | forceload the P4 area X 1090 to 1130, Z 1170 to 1220; clear its generated animals (not a row)
> forceload add 1090 1170 1130 1220
sleep 5
> kill @e[type=!minecraft:player,x=1090,y=-64,z=1170,dx=40,dy=40,dz=50]
sleep 2

